<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo ends firmer vs mark, seen higher.</title>
<headline>Escudo ends firmer vs mark, seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo closed firmer against the mark, reflecting a stronger peseta, franc and dollar and demand for the Portuguese currency by foreign investors planning to buy Lisbon stocks, notably Electricidade de Portugal. Dealers said pressure from foreign investors could push up the value of the escudo tomorrow. The escudo closed at 100.72/75 per mark, compared with 100.92/95 at the opening.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
